<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="Claude" version="26.0.0">
  <diagram name="AI Gateway - Agent Identity, CIE and Entra ID" id="aigw-agent-identity">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1760" pageHeight="1404" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="title" value="How an agent&#39;s identity reaches the AI Gateway" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="18" width="1000" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Entra ID does three different jobs here, on three different clocks. Cloud Identity Engine does one of them. Separating them is most of the answer." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="50" width="1200" height="22" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ LEFT COLUMN ============ -->

        <mxCell id="myth" value="&lt;b&gt;There is no User-ID here.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;User-ID is a PAN-OS mechanism. The firewall learns an &lt;i&gt;IP-to-user mapping&lt;/i&gt; out of band, from a domain controller or an agent, and security policy then matches on the user it found.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The AI Gateway has none of that. No IP-to-user mapping, no User-ID agent, and no directory group travelling on the request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Identity arrives inside the request, as the credential itself.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;So the question to ask is not &quot;how do I turn on User-ID&quot;. It is &lt;b&gt;which credential does the agent present, and what identity does that credential carry&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#ef4444;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="96" width="312" height="300" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="roleshdr" value="The three jobs Entra ID does" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="418" width="312" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="roles" value="&lt;b&gt;1. Source directory, behind CIE.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Supplies the users and groups that become workspace membership. Runs on a sync schedule, not per request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Token issuer for the agent.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Signs the JWT the agent presents. The gateway validates it against Entra&#39;s JWKS. This is per request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Egress credential to Azure.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;A service principal or managed identity the gateway uses to reach Azure AI Foundry. Nothing to do with the caller.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#006DCC&quot;&gt;All three can be the same Entra tenant. They are still three separate configurations.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="438" width="312" height="316" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="credhdr" value="What each credential attributes to" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="776" width="312" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="creds" value="&lt;b&gt;Service API key&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Shared, not tied to a person. The request attributes to the application. Split further only with metadata you set yourself.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;User API key&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Tied to one directory-provisioned member. The user picker only lists people CIE has already synced into that workspace.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;JWT from your IdP&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The gateway reads identity from the claims, in this precedence order:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;email_id&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;sub&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;uid&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="796" width="312" height="300" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="choosehdr" value="Which one an agent should use" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1204" width="520" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="choose" value="&lt;b&gt;Unattended, no human behind it&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; a Service API key per agent, with metadata naming the agent. There is no person to attribute to, so do not pretend there is one.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Acting for a signed-in person&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; a JWT carrying that person&#39;s email. Attribution and the workspace role both follow the human.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;A named service account you want in the member list&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; a User API key issued against a CIE-provisioned user." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="36" y="1226" width="520" height="142" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ BAND 1 - CONTROL PLANE ============ -->

        <mxCell id="band1" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#66CCEE;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="380" y="96" width="1344" height="258" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="band1lbl" value="1 &#183; CONTROL PLANE &#8212; who belongs to which workspace" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="398" y="110" width="700" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="band1clock" value="runs on a schedule, never on the request path" style="text;html=1;align=right;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#006DCC;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="110" width="456" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="c1" value="&lt;b&gt;Entra ID&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your directory of users and groups.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Okta and on-prem AD sit here too.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="142" width="236" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c2" value="&lt;b&gt;Cloud Identity Engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Aggregates and caches the directories you connect.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;SCM &#8594; Cloud Identity Engine &#8594; Directory Sync&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3F7FF;strokeColor=#66CCEE;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="142" width="236" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c3" value="&lt;b&gt;Directory Sync&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pick the Connected Directory and the &lt;b&gt;User Identity Attribute&lt;/b&gt;: UPN or Mail.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;AI Gateway &#8594; Admin Settings &#8594; Authentication&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3F7FF;strokeColor=#66CCEE;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="920" y="142" width="236" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b&gt;Group &#8594; Workspace&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A 1:1 mapping. One group to one workspace, one workspace to one group.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;The workspace must already exist.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E3F7FF;strokeColor=#66CCEE;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1180" y="142" width="236" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c5" value="&lt;b&gt;Workspace members&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Provisioned and deprovisioned for you as group membership changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#22c55e&quot;&gt;This list is what a User API key can be issued against.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1440" y="142" width="236" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="a12" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c1" target="c2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a23" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c2" target="c3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a34" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c3" target="c4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="a45" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="band1note" value="&lt;b&gt;Timing&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; delta sync every 15 minutes, so a group change takes up to 15 minutes to land. CIE rebuilds its cache roughly weekly and the gateway full-syncs automatically; &lt;b&gt;Full Sync&lt;/b&gt; forces it. &#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160; &lt;b&gt;Scope&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; CIE Directory Sync is for SCM tenants. A non-SCM deployment uses SCIM provisioning instead." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="282" width="1300" height="56" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ JOIN CALLOUT ============ -->

        <mxCell id="join" value="&lt;b&gt;Where the two halves meet, and the one string that has to match&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;When the email on the agent&#39;s token matches an AI Gateway user in the target workspace, the request is attributed to &lt;b&gt;that person&lt;/b&gt; and inherits their workspace role. When it does not match, the request falls back to a generic workspace service key and the per-user attribution is lost.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ef4444&quot;&gt;That comparison is a plain string match. The &lt;b&gt;User Identity Attribute&lt;/b&gt; you chose in Directory Sync (UPN or Mail) has to produce the same value as the email claim Entra puts in the token. Choose &lt;b&gt;Mail&lt;/b&gt; when the UPN is &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;user@tenant.onmicrosoft.com&lt;/font&gt; but the real address is not.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#f59e0b;strokeWidth=3;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="380" y="376" width="1344" height="138" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ BAND 2 - DATA PLANE ============ -->

        <mxCell id="band2" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#66CCEE;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="380" y="536" width="1344" height="396" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="band2lbl" value="2 &#183; DATA PLANE &#8212; the agent call itself" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="398" y="550" width="700" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="band2clock" value="every single request" style="text;html=1;align=right;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#006DCC;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="550" width="456" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="d1" value="&lt;b&gt;The agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A workload, not a person at a browser. It holds a client ID and a secret, or a managed identity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Registered as an app in the Azure portal.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#00294D;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="584" width="212" height="222" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="d2" value="&lt;b&gt;Entra ID issues a token&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Signed &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;RS256&lt;/font&gt;, carrying &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;iss&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;aud&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;sub&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;exp&lt;/font&gt;, and an email claim.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sent to the gateway as &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;Authorization: Bearer&lt;/font&gt;, or in &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;x-portkey-api-key&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;The gateway never sees the agent&#39;s secret.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="584" width="212" height="222" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gwbox" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#FFB81C;strokeWidth=3;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="880" y="572" width="824" height="248" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gwlbl" value="Prisma AIRS AI Gateway" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#00294D;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="584" width="400" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="g1" value="&lt;b&gt;Validate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Signature against the JWKS, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;kid&lt;/font&gt; match, &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;exp&lt;/font&gt; in the future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;JWKS: the Entra &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;discovery/v2.0/keys&lt;/font&gt; endpoint for your tenant.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=9;fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="896" y="610" width="192" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g2" value="&lt;b&gt;Resolve org and workspace&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Org: &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;portkey_oid&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;organisation_id&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; the single org in &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ORGANISATIONS_TO_SYNC&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Workspace: &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;portkey_workspace&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;workspace_slug&lt;/font&gt; &#8594; deployment default." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=9;fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1098" y="610" width="192" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g3" value="&lt;b&gt;Check scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each route needs its own scope:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;completions.write&lt;/font&gt; for chat&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;agents.invoke&lt;/font&gt; for agents&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;mcp.invoke&lt;/font&gt; for MCP&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Missing scope returns 403.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=9;fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1300" y="610" width="192" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="g4" value="&lt;b&gt;Attribute the request&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Identity taken from &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;email_id&lt;/font&gt;, then &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;sub&lt;/font&gt;, then &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;uid&lt;/font&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Then budgets, rate limits and policies apply, exactly as they would for an API key.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#22c55e&quot;&gt;This is what lands in the logs.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f0fdf4;strokeColor=#22c55e;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=9;fontSize=10.5;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1502" y="610" width="192" height="196" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="ad12" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#006DCC;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="d1" target="d2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ad2g" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#E5A300;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="d2" target="gwbox"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ag12" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#3b82f6;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="g1" target="g2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ag23" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#3b82f6;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="g2" target="g3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ag34" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#3b82f6;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="g3" target="g4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="band2note" value="&lt;b&gt;Where validation runs&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; on AI Gateway Cloud the management plane validates the token. A hybrid or air-gapped gateway can validate locally with &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_ENABLED=ON&lt;/font&gt; on gateway 2.5.0 or later, which keeps authentication working when the management plane is unreachable. &#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160; &lt;b&gt;Mode A&lt;/b&gt; is for when you control the token issuer and can add the gateway&#39;s own claims. &lt;b&gt;Mode B&lt;/b&gt; is the Entra case: a stock IdP token, with org, workspace and scopes resolved on the gateway instead. Use &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;JWT_LOCAL_AUTH_DEFAULT_SCOPES&lt;/font&gt; when you cannot add scopes in Entra.&#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160; &lt;b&gt;Entra values&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; JWKS &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant-id}/discovery/v2.0/keys&lt;/font&gt;, issuer &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant-id}/v2.0&lt;/font&gt;, audience &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;{client-id}&lt;/font&gt;." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="844" width="1300" height="90" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ BAND 3 - EGRESS ============ -->

        <mxCell id="band3" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#66CCEE;strokeWidth=2;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="380" y="954" width="1344" height="228" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="band3lbl" value="3 &#183; EGRESS &#8212; how the gateway reaches the provider" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="398" y="968" width="700" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="band3clock" value="a separate credential the agent never sees" style="text;html=1;align=right;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#006DCC;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="968" width="456" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="e1" value="&lt;b&gt;AI Gateway&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Swaps the caller&#39;s credential for the provider&#39;s.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Two independent layers.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#E5A300;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="1000" width="212" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2" value="&lt;b&gt;Azure AI Foundry&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;or Azure OpenAI&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In your own subscription, billed on your own meter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#666666&quot;&gt;Role on the resource:&lt;br&gt;Cognitive Services OpenAI User&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e7f3ff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="700" y="1000" width="236" height="124" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e3" value="&lt;b&gt;The three auth types the integration form accepts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Resource API key&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; the static secret. Simplest, and the one to move away from.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Azure Managed Entity&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; a managed identity plus its Managed ClientID. No secret to store.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Azure Entra ID&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; ClientID, Secret and Tenant ID for a service principal.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#22c55e&quot;&gt;Keyless is possible on the Azure side. The static resource key is a choice, not a requirement.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f7f8fa;strokeColor=#dee2e6;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=10;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1024" y="992" width="680" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="ae12" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#E5A300;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="e1" target="e2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ae23" style="endArrow=none;html=1;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#dee2e6;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="e2" target="e3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="band3note" value="The agent authenticates to the gateway. The gateway authenticates to Azure. Neither credential is ever visible to the other side, which is the whole point of putting the gateway in the path." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400" y="1140" width="1300" height="30" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <!-- ============ PITFALLS ============ -->

        <mxCell id="pithdr" value="Six things that silently break this" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#666666;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="1204" width="700" height="18" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pitfalls" value="&lt;b&gt;1.&lt;/b&gt;&#160; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;RS256&lt;/font&gt; only. An &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;HS256&lt;/font&gt; token is rejected, and the error reads as a bad API key rather than a bad algorithm.&#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160;&lt;b&gt;2.&lt;/b&gt;&#160; The &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;kid&lt;/font&gt; in the token header must match a key in the configured JWKS.&#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160;&lt;b&gt;3.&lt;/b&gt;&#160; &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;exp&lt;/font&gt; is mandatory; a token without one never authenticates.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4.&lt;/b&gt;&#160; A user whose chosen identity attribute is empty in CIE is skipped during sync, with no error on the request that later fails to attribute.&#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160;&lt;b&gt;5.&lt;/b&gt;&#160; Deleting a group mapping removes those users from the workspace immediately, and the mapping does not come back by re-enabling sync.&#160;&#160;&#8226;&#160;&#160;&lt;b&gt;6.&lt;/b&gt;&#160; On a multi-org gateway a token with no org claim is rejected with a 401; set a single org in &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;ORGANISATIONS_TO_SYNC&lt;/font&gt; or add &lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;portkey_oid&lt;/font&gt; to the token." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#E5A300;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=12;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="1226" width="1144" height="142" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
